Is current workflow is "cut model" -> "pack to comfyui format"


• Yes. The current workflow is essentially:

  Full compatible Mistral Small 3.2 checkpoint
      ↓
  Cut/prune to embedding + transformer layers 0–29
      ↓
  Remove layers 30–39, final norm, LM head, vision tower, and projector
      ↓
  Rename Hugging Face keys:
  language_model.model.* → model.*
      ↓
  Embed tekken.json as the uint8 tensor tekken_model
      ↓
  Package everything into one standalone .safetensors file
      ↓
  Load from ComfyUI/models/text_encoders/

  So it performs two operations:

  1. Model pruning: retains only the components FLUX.2 uses for hidden states 10, 20, and 30.
  2. ComfyUI packaging: rewrites keys and embeds the tokenizer in ComfyUI’s expected standalone format.

  It does not retrain, fine-tune, quantize, or fundamentally convert the causal LLM architecture into a different encoder
  architecture. ComfyUI simply uses the pruned transformer as a hidden-state text encoder.
